  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Mepartricin is an antifungal antibiotic used for local treatment of fungal infections of the mouth, skin, and genital/urinary tract, and also for benign prostatic hypertrophy. It is considered investigational and is not an authorised medicine in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q104708340&quot;>Wikidata Q104708340</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>mepartricin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A01AB16, D01AA06, G01AA09, G04CX03</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13633&quot;>DB13633</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/11981152&quot;>11981152</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q104708340&quot;>Q104708340</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C119H174N4O38</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>2268.69 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
